ng one would create false security; an invalid/revoked key still returns 401 rather than silently downgrading to anonymous, so a real integration bug (typo'd env var, revoked key) isn't hidden."}, {"id": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_auth_persite_credential_model", "label": "Per-Site trackingId/apiSecret Auth Model", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "crm-agencyos/backend/EXTERNAL_API_DOCUMENTATION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Website Intelligence needs a distinct matching credential pair per tracked site, not one global key, because it must attribute a lead to that specific site's visitor/session/UTM data rather than just authenticate a generic caller."}], "edges": [{"source": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_lead_sync", "target": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_auth_api_key_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "crm-agencyos/backend/EXTERNAL_API_DOCUMENTATION.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_lead_capture", "target": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_auth_optional_key_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "crm-agencyos/backend/EXTERNAL_API_DOCUMENTATION.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_website_intelligence", "target": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_auth_persite_credential_model", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "crm-agencyos/backend/EXTERNAL_API_DOCUMENTATION.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_lead_sync", "target": "crm_agencyos_backend_external_api_documentation_lead_capture", "relation